{"id":"vorrat","lemma":"Vorrat","pos":"noun","rank":3659,"glosses":["supply, stock, store, reserve"],"ipa":"/ˈfoː(r)ˌraːt/","audio":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/4/42/De-Vorrat.ogg/De-Vorrat.ogg.mp3","gender":"m","forms":{"genitive":"Vorrates","plural":"Vorräte"},"examples":[{"text":"Wir brauchen neue Vorräte.","en":"I need some new supplies.","words":[{"g":"we"},{"g":"to need"},{"g":"new","l":"neu"},null]},{"text":"Die Vorräte gehen langsam aus.","en":"The supplies are beginning to give out.","words":[{"g":"the"},null,{"g":"to go, to walk"},{"g":"slowly"},{"g":"out of / from"}]},{"text":"Wir haben einen Vorrat an Toilettenpapier.","en":"We have a stock of toilet paper.","words":[{"g":"we"},{"g":"have"},{"g":"a","l":"ein"},null,{"g":"at / on"},{"g":"toilet paper"}]},{"text":"Ich bin hier, um Vorräte zu kaufen.","en":"I'm here to buy supplies.","words":[{"g":"I"},{"g":"am","l":"sein"},{"g":"here"},{"g":"around / at"},null,{"g":"to / too"},{"g":"to buy, to purchase"}]},{"text":"Unser Vorrat geht langsam zur Neige.","en":"Our supplies are running low.","words":[{"g":"our"},null,{"g":"to go, to walk","l":"gehen"},{"g":"slowly"},{"g":"to the"},{"g":"to incline","l":"neigen"}]}]}